# Generated
report_*.json
logs/
# **A core dump, not the file named `core.md`.** Without the leading slash this pattern matched
# `docs/reference/packages/core.md` - the reference page for the `core` package - so the page was invisible to
# `git add -A` and a push built from the index deleted it from the remote.
/core.*
tests/benchmarks/real-world/.stress-data/

# **Third-party corpora are fetched, never committed.** A dataset in the tree is a dataset nobody can date: the CoSQA
# files live in the repository that publishes them and the workflow downloads them per run, recording the SHA-256 in
# the artifact. Committing them would also put somebody else's licence inside this one.
benchmarks/corpora/

# Local working files from scripts/callgraph-quality.ts (the JSON record is committed, the dumps are not).
.callgraph-quality/

# **Where the dead-code workflow stages one half of its record before uploading it.** `upload-artifact` archives a single
# matched file at the root of the artifact, so the job copies the record into a directory whose name the gate job then
# names explicitly. Local runs may leave it behind; it is never the record, only a copy of one.
artifact/
